# Locally installed tool binaries (protoc-gen-go, protoc-gen-go-grpc, buf).
# Provisioned by `make tools`, never committed.
bin/

# Go module cache and build cache, scoped to this directory so that building
# Sekizui never writes outside it (D34).
.gocache/

# Local overrides — may contain real target refs or credential paths.
*.local.yaml
*.local.yml
# A local configuration DIRECTORY (D278): the shared document symlinked in,
# plus the local additions. Ignored whole, symlink included.
*.local.d/
.env
.env.*

# WAL spill and local audit sink output from dev runs.
*.wal
audit-*.jsonl
audit*.jsonl
*.p12
*.pfx
.netrc

# Compiled binaries from `go build -o`. `make build` writes nothing here (it
# only populates .gocache), but building cmd/sekizui by hand lands a binary at
# the repo root, and a stray 30 MB executable in a PR is noise. One entry per
# directory under cmd/ — the list named two of five, and a 17 MB sekizui-tap
# was committed through the gap (found at the 2026-09-28 Feierabend).
/sekizui
/sekizui-devcert
/sekizui-mcpspec
/sekizui-refsnap
/sekizui-tap

# Go test and profiling artifacts. `go test -c` emits *.test; -coverprofile and
# the pprof outputs land as *.out / *.prof. The §12.1 Rego throughput spike is
# specifically a benchmarking exercise, so these WILL appear.
*.test
*.out
*.prof
*.pprof

# Service-account keys. Credentials belong in a secret manager and configuration
# carries only references (§4.7) — but P2 brings GCP Secret Manager work, and a
# downloaded key file is the one mistake that is unrecoverable once pushed.
# Deliberately broad: a false positive costs an explicit `git add -f`, a false
# negative costs a credential rotation.
*service-account*.json
*credentials*.json
*-sa.json
*.pem
*.key

# Acceptance-run output. Regenerated by `make acceptance`; the artifact is for
# reading, not for committing — a stale copy in the tree would be worse than none.
/out/

# macOS.
.DS_Store

# Locally generated development CA and mTLS identities (make dev-certs).
# Regenerate rather than share; they expire in 30 days by design.
/dev/
